// D1567 — the value is a CALL to an un-annotated function whose every returned value is a
// bare `null`. The checker types that return `TyPrim:null` — the `null` TYPE, not a nullable
// of anything — so every producer in the inferred-return recorder declined, `fRetKind` kept
// its `"i32"` default, and the body's own `null` reached `emitNullLitNode` with no seed at
// all: a loud reject on a `vl check`-clean program, at every delivery position.
//
// The rep is `nullref` (`(ref null none)`), the bottom of the GC hierarchy — one value, and
// a subtype of every nullable ref valtype, which is what lets one result serve a struct /
// string / list / map / closure destination with no coercion.
//
// The PROOF reads THROUGH the narrow (`v.a`), so a cell whose result came back at the wrong
// heap type traps or refuses rather than passing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type C = { a: i32, b: i32 }
function __np() {
  return null
}
// @@VALUE@@
__np()
// @@TYPE@@
C | null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v.a)
// @@MISS@@
print("none")
// @@WANT@@
none
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: a map whose VALUE is `null` cannot be told from a missing key — the read's `!= null` guard is false either way, so the proof prints nothing at both seeds
